  "rules": [
    "Rich text: *words* become italic emphasis and **words** become bold, in fields used as headings and captions.",
    "Nine notes, always: three top, three heart, three base. The scroll timeline is nine steps; only names, colours and text change.",
    "notes.*.share must add up to 100 (they are the formula's proportions).",
    "product.concentration must sit inside the chosen concentrationType's range (cologne 2-5, toilette 5-15, parfum 15-20, extrait 20-30).",
    "Prices are whole numbers with the currency written before them; the per-wear and per-ml figures use a full stop for decimals.",
    "Phone nav: business.short (26px) and the buy button (\"Shop 50 ml · $140\", 13px) share one row with the sound button. Together they must fit a 375px phone; the original fits with about 4px to spare.",
    "business.name is the full trading name (page title, hero line, footer); business.short is the form used where space is tight (nav, the etched bottle label).",
    "product.name is the fragrance name exactly as the brand writes it (hero title, page text); product.short is the form shown in the HUD and etched on the bottle, where space is tight. Long words in the hero title shrink the title to fit."
  ]
